{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "10532",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10532",
  "key": "AIN-209",
  "fields": {
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User explicitly requested removing all pipeline invocations from submission services and clarified: stop processing entirely; save input without pipeline execution. Backend-only change to existing manual entry workflow, linked to AIN-95; no new UI controls or layout. Existing AIN-183/184 boundary/creator and AIN-205 versioned evidence are reuse dependencies, not broader completion claims."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance: validate supplied manual fields and atomically save envelope plus immutable, versioned user input without normalization/schema-generation execution or pipeline schema validation. Create no pipeline runs, artifacts, stage executions, ingestion events or jobs. Preserve incomplete drafts, authenticated tenant/personal ownership, original values and read-only workbench/board access. Keep existing pipeline evidence readable. Do not silently move execution into a route or another workflow. Existing explicit document processing remains separate. Pipeline schema eligibility and downstream pricing are not certified by manual save."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Required sequence: AIN-48/50/51 ownership/version slice (submission-owned immutable initial input, current edits still owned by feedback) -> additive input migration AIN-54 slice -> creation/read adapters -> real PostgreSQL isolation, rollback, concurrency and zero-execution assertions -> final API format/check and affected tests. Preserve old input/evidence; no fabricated backfill. No deployment or package publication required for local implementation. Existing broader AIN-3/95/2/18/48/50/51/54 criteria remain incomplete. Exclude ingestion/search orchestration, regeneration comparison UI, board pagination, identity claiming and finance workflows because not prerequisites to stopping manual execution. No UI source change intended; backend integration evidence rather than artificial UI stories.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
